    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Geophysical inversion techniques are used to invert surface deformation measurements for geometric and incremental growth of shallow hydraulic fractures. It is shown that fracture opening is highly non-uniform,and very shallow hydraulic fracturing is essentially a stable process. This information is useful in evaluating the performance and efficiency of hydraulic fractures.",
